# p2 has args but no returns: "for _, tt := range tests {" (because it uses tt.args)
# p1 has no args and no returns: "for range tests {" (because it doesn't use tt at all)

# So the rule for "for range tests" vs "for _, tt := range tests":
# If the test struct has ONLY "name string" (no args, no returns, no receiver fields):
